minor spoilers. (not really.  but just in case)

Unremarkable, but weird game.  1 Scroll of light, and under 6 scrolls
of identify throughout the entire game.  Found a wand of wishing within the
first 10 levels.

In the end, my Barbarian had Hp=135, Ac=-7 (Gray Dragon Scale mail), Str=25,
Dx=15, Co=18, In=8, Wi=5 (-2 helm of brilliance :-(  Didn't catch it until
after I ascended.) and Ch=6.

No wands to speak of (except wishing), no spells, useful intrinsics were
teleport, invisibility and see invisible. The only things that got me 
through were a rustproof Excalibur, Stormbringer, Gray Dragon Scale mail,
rings of conflict and teleport control.

Some of my deaths have been as fun as this particular win, but none have
been as satisfying. 

Once again, I don't think we need to be so conservative when making
recommendations to others who don't know if they're ready for the castle
level or not.  We don't need > 150 Hp and < -12 AC.  Invisibility and
a ring of conflict can take you pretty far.

